A1. What was Cleopatra's ticket to another world? ~ ASP
A4. What do they call a girl who marries in France? ~ MADAM
A9. What gambol and are often fleeced? ~ LAMBS
A14. What does Judge, Jr., do to drown his troubles? ~ POUR
A16. In what are X-word puzzles solved? (slang). ~ DOMES
A18. Give an abbreviation for a science in which Mr. Chas. A. Lindbergh is skilled. ~ AERO
A19. Give a name for a book in which maps are kept. ~ ALBUM
A21. From what root is evil supposed to spring? ~ MONEY
A23. What did Adam lose when he got married? ~ RIB
A24. What do big business men belong to? (Abbr) ~ GO
A25. What are Scandinavian myths? ~ SAGAS
A26. What do all nations say they fight for? ~ PEACE
A28. What is an abbreviation for "overhead"? ~ OER
A30. Give a good old-fashioned girl's name. ~ AMY
A32. What do people use if they want to get ahead quickly? ~ GAS
A33. Give another name for a vamp. ~ SNAKE
A36. What is the opening remark of a jackass? ~ HE
A37. What is a call for help? ~ SOS
A38. What was immortalized by Elinor Glyn? ~ IT
A39. Give a masculine name. ~ RUSSEL
A41. Name a drink carrier of the good old days. ~ PAIL
A43. Name a well-known white house. ~ IGLOO
A44. What kind of wolf resides in Africa? ~ AARD
A45. What does a lone wolf go by? ~ ITSELF
A46. What are the Roman numerals for 510? ~ DX
A47. What is Florida in the Summer time? ~ HOT
A48. Where is many a poor fish caught? (Abbr.) ~ NS
A49. What is a good thing to get a light with in the wind? ~ FUSEE
A52. What verb means "to make free"? ~ RID
A53. Name a great American poet. ~ POE
A55. Name a center around which things revolve. ~ HUB
A57. What will get your jack if you don't watch out? (Plural.) ~ KINGS
A59. Name a famous bucket. ~ OAKEN
A60. What is sob stuff? ~ WO
A61. Name a girl whose age is subject to controversy. ~ ANN
A62. What is Ziegfeld's stock in trade? ~ GIRLS
A64. What gets terribly, terribly hurt when thrown down? ~ RIDER
A66. What does the landlord do to the house? ~ LETS
A68. Name an Englishman who was famous for his papers. ~ ROGER
A70. Who was the first boy to go wrong? ~ CAIN
A71. What is New Jersey famous for? ~ PESTS
A72. Name a famous German resort. ~ BADEN
A73. What is the goad of all Misses'? ~ MRS

D1. What adverb refers to things in motion? ~ APAGE
D2. What is always played alone? ~ SOLO
D3. Name an English filling station. ~ PUB
D5. What is Lib's first name? ~ AD
D6. What is another name for a dominion? ~ DOMAIN
D7. Name one of the prophets. ~ AMOS
D8. What are the great open spaces supposed to be particularly productive of? ~ MEN
D10. What abbreviation means an association of arts? ~ AA
D11. What was Grandma's cuss word? ~ MERCY
D12. Name a very cheesy cheese. ~ BRIE
D13. What kind of story is used by panhandlers? ~ SOB
D15. What do errant husbands resort to to square themselves with their wives? ~ RUSES
D17. Name a month with a famous morning. (Abbr.) ~ SEP
D20. What did Tunney do to Dempsey? ~ MAR
D22. Name a solemn affirmative. ~ YEA
D27. What Biblical name means "a burden"? (The middle letter is A) ~ AMASA
D28. What is Cuba to the U. S. A.? ~ OASIS
D29. What are the letters of approval? ~ OK
D31. What is the open country of South Africa? ~ VELDT
D32. What are always butting in? ~ GOATS
D33. What is an unbending person? ~ STIFF
D34. Where can anybody see the world? ~ ATLAS
D35. What word means to gnaw off? ~ ERODE
D36. Name an ancient king. ~ HEROD
D37. What is back of every successful man? ~ SPINE
D40. What is a gentleman in India? ~ SAHIB
D42. What is always yellow? ~ LEMON
D50. Name the world's largest (nominally) dry area. (Abbr.) ~ US
D51. What did the wise man do when he made an error? ~ ERASED
D52. What could you call Norse poetry? ~ RUNIC
D53. What are often carried on the hip? (Plural.) ~ PINTS
D54. What is yellow on the inside ? ~ EGG
D55. Name a pronoun. ~ HER
D56. What do both autos and cows wear? ~ HORNS
D57. What joint is usually exposed these days? ~ KNEE
D58. Name a title of respect often used disrespectfully ~ SIR
D59. What is a Russian given name? (Feminine) ~ OLGA
D60. What is just another damn thing? ~ WEIR
D61. What wears a white cap? ~ ALP
D63. What is a good nickname for a stick-up man? ~ ROB
D65. What retards the flow of liquid? ~ DAM
D67. What is Broadway? (Abbr.) ~ ST
D69. Name a note in the musical scale. ~ RE


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A73: What is the goad of all Misses'? → possibly 'goal' (printed 'goad')
D15: What do errant husbands resort to to square themselves with their wives? → resort to square (printed 'resort to to square')

